            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n`MiniFiles.open()` by default uses current working directory as anchor (target) directory. When you open `nvim dotfiles/config/nvim`, `MiniFiles.open()` is called with `'dotfiles/config/nvim'` path, but when you later call it (probably without arguments), it is called without arguments and uses current working directory (which by default is the one Neovim was opened in; `~` in your case).\r\n\r\nYou have several options:\r\n- Create a 'mini.files' mapping which changes current working directory to the one inside which cursor is located. Here is [an example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2b37c5e1d2a3f62ba4060a819f17d8d976018928/doc/mini-files.txt#L451).\r\n- Use automated change of current working directory. For example, [`MiniMisc.setup_auto_root()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2b37c5e1d2a3f62ba4060a819f17d8d976018928/doc/mini-misc.txt#L119) from 'mini.misc'.\r\n- Manually change current working directory to the one you'd like.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
